WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.609
Silently passing through the inky void of
space, a vessel was hurriedly making its way

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:07.490
towards its destination.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.010
The craft was sleek, designed and built by
hands not of this world.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:16.699
Aboard, one of the occupants knelt before
its elders: it was time.

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:22.090
It gathered its arsenal in a methodical, almost
ceremonial fashion; its spear latched onto

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:27.500
its back with its survival gear, a MediKit,
containing surgical equipment and specialized

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.500
serums.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.820
It donned its gauntlets, then reached for
the final piece: its mask, that it slipped

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.379
over its face.

00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:39.640
Ready for its task, the creature boarded a
smaller scout ship, which was jettisoned and

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.980
began to descend towards the planet below:
a world known as ‘Earth’.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:50.430
On the surface of the planet itself, a technician
was sitting at his desk, bored, staring at

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:55.300
readouts from satellites and the endless sweeping
of a radar, scanning the skies above for any

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.020
signs of disturbance.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:01.289
For a moment, as the scout craft passed through
the atmosphere, something happened that broke

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:02.800
the technician out of his boredom.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.260
There was a blip on the radar, the tiny detection
of an unknown signal, that of an object traveling

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.759
on a direct course through the sky.

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:17.020
Just as the technician started to take notice,
the approaching ship activated a stealth mechanism,

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.970
reflecting all light away from it in order
to render it almost invisible, while simultaneously

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:24.540
becoming undetectable to radar.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.520
The blip vanished from the screen and didn’t
reappear.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.549
The technician shrugged, thinking it was probably
nothing but an equipment glitch; besides,

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:37.110
the SCP Foundation didn’t pay him enough
to follow up on every tiny blip.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:42.470
A few hours later, and several continents
away, a Mobile Task Force was on an assignment.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:47.360
The oppressive heat and humidity of the Lacandon
Jungle was bearing down on them; especially

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.969
in their combat gear, the operatives were
all feeling unbearably hot.

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:56.120
The Foundation researchers overseeing the
MTF’s mission via satellite didn’t have

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.680
to contend with the elements in the comfort
of their air-conditioned command center.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:05.310
But little did they or their boots on the
ground know, there was something else visiting

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.009
the rainforest too.

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:12.350
It had been stalking the squad for a few miles
now, and not one of them had noticed…

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.030
just as the creature planned.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:19.530
A trio of red laser beams cast three distinct
dots over one of the MTF operative’s chest…

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.760
Suddenly, a streak of energy shot through
the air, crackling as it struck the agent,

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.640
tearing through his chest and killing him
on the spot.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.430
Instinctively, the remaining troops turned
and opened fire at the treetop where the blast

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:34.850
had come from, spraying a volley of bullets
enough to start shredding the wood of the

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.840
tree, splinters, and bark raining down.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:43.790
They hit nothing, there was no sign of whoever
or whatever had fired that shot and killed

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.130
their teammate.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:49.480
From behind them, a pair of discs with a row
of long, fan-like blades around their edge

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:50.569
flew through the air.

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:54.950
There was so much force behind the arm that
threw them that the pair of shuriken lifted

00:02:54.950 --> 00:03:00.129
two of the remaining MTF soldiers off their
feet and impaled them to the trunks of nearby

00:03:00.129 --> 00:03:01.129
trees.

00:03:01.129 --> 00:03:05.600
The last remaining Foundation operative looked
at the bodies of his dead squad mates in horror,

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.519
before turning and fleeing.

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:10.849
But just as he ran for his life, something
caught him.

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:16.269
It was transparent, cloaked, and near-impossible
to see, but it had plunged a pair of blades

00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:21.540
into the MTF troop’s chest, lifting him
off his feet with ease as he screamed in pain.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:27.239
An invisible, leathery-skinned hand reached
for his throat and twisted, and in an instant,

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:32.420
with a sickening crack, the man was silent,
dropped limply to the floor.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:36.860
From the command center, watching in awe as
this imperceptible monster tore through four

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:41.590
of their finest operatives with ease, a pair
of researchers turned to look at each other.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:46.439
The expressions they both wore were faces
of sheer disbelief; they had both heard the

00:03:46.439 --> 00:03:48.970
stories, instantly recognizing the destructive
behavior.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.840
But never thought they’d see – or not
see – it carried out for real.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.569
“We still don’t have a name for them,
do we?”

00:03:56.569 --> 00:04:00.160
Researcher Hall asked as the pair of them
walked briskly down the corridor.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.140
“Negative,” replied his counterpart, Researcher
DiLiegro.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.709
“But the files we acquired from military
intelligence suggest that they’ve been coming

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:08.379
to Earth for decades.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:12.049
Centuries even, the earliest known encounter
took place in the 1700s.”

00:04:12.049 --> 00:04:14.209
“Can we negotiate with this one at all?”

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:16.430
Hall asked, fully expecting the answer.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:20.500
“I don’t think they respond well to that
kind of engagement,” DiLiegro said.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.820
“They seemingly come to Earth with one singular
purpose: to hunt.”

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.130
“For sport?”

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:27.190
“It seems so.”

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.530
“What about their capabilities?”

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.039
the senior researcher pressed.

00:04:31.039 --> 00:04:35.070
“Their technology is pretty advanced, even
compared to some of the things we’ve seen,”

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.070
the other explained.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:39.509
“On top of that, they’re fast, strong,
and completely ruthless.

00:04:39.509 --> 00:04:41.270
Pretty much an apex predator.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:44.850
According to intel, the instances of these
creatures that have previously visited Earth

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.009
have displayed a sort of… tribal nature.”

00:04:47.009 --> 00:04:48.190
“Care to elaborate?”

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.190
Hall probed.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:53.350
“Based on the files, their hunts seem partially
recreational.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:59.039
But also like some kind of ritual, to prove
themselves as capable or to challenge themselves.”

00:04:59.039 --> 00:05:02.009
“That gives me an idea,” the researcher
replied.

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:04.490
“Contact Containment Area 25b.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:08.349
If we play this right, we can bag one of these
creatures and bring it in for testing.”

00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:11.259
***
Time seemed to race by as Hall and DiLiegro

00:05:11.259 --> 00:05:17.040
were bundled aboard a transport and taken
directly to Containment Area 25b; a facility

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:22.039
built by the Foundation specifically to house
a particularly dangerous anomaly.

00:05:22.039 --> 00:05:26.400
Within the hour, the two researchers were
standing facing a huge stone cube, its dark

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.389
surface sporting a number of symbols engraved
into it.

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:33.979
Growing impatient, knowing their window of
opportunity was rapidly closing, Hall turned

00:05:33.979 --> 00:05:38.139
to one of the Foundation personnel stationed
within the Primary Containment Zone around

00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:39.139
SCP-076.

00:05:39.139 --> 00:05:41.050
“Play it again,” he instructed.

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:43.539
“Wake him up.”

00:05:43.539 --> 00:05:47.889
Hitting a button, a recorded message began
to play over the facility’s loudspeakers.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:52.669
It had been translated into an ancient Sumerian
dialect that the entity within the stone cube

00:05:52.669 --> 00:05:55.100
had historically shown a preference for.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.130
“Come on out,” the message stated.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:00.169
“We know you don’t think any of us are
worth your time.

00:06:00.169 --> 00:06:02.410
But we remember Omega Seven.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:07.259
You’ve agreed to work with us before, even
though you don’t think we present enough

00:06:07.259 --> 00:06:09.150
of a challenge to you.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.610
But we may have found something that will.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:15.360
An adversary that you could have the privilege
of besting in combat.”

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.550
There was a brief moment of silence, before
the stone began to rumble.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:24.759
The security personnel on site tensed up,
gripping their weapons in shaky, nervous hands.

00:06:24.759 --> 00:06:29.479
Slowly, the circular lock on the side of the
cube began twisting, the door it kept sealed

00:06:29.479 --> 00:06:30.509
beginning to open.

00:06:30.509 --> 00:06:33.960
“Are you sure we can do this, Hall?” asked
DiLiegro.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:38.610
“If SCP-076 isn’t willing to cooperate,
this could go south really quickly.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.490
And god forbid, what if somebody found out
what we’re having him do?”

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:46.229
Hall didn’t answer, instead watching as
the door to the cube finally opened, and a

00:06:46.229 --> 00:06:48.889
lean man in his late twenties stepped out.

00:06:48.889 --> 00:06:53.580
His grey eyes stared out under a mess of jet
black hair, his body adorned with tattoos

00:06:53.580 --> 00:07:00.080
of arcane runes and occult imagery, the sneering
faces of demons, over his olive skin.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.650
As the guards around him nervously raised
their weapons at the ready, SCP-076-2 casually

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:10.120
strode up to Researcher Hall, until the two
were inches away from each other.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:11.120
“Where?”

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.360
Able asked.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.400
Fitting him with a communication earpiece
and having him board a transport, Able was

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:21.840
sent directly towards the last known coordinates
of the now-deceased MTF, deep in the heart

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:23.680
of the Lacandon Jungle.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:28.509
Sat atop a tree as the aircraft made its approach,
the creature had lowered its cloaking device,

00:07:28.509 --> 00:07:32.860
certain it was alone as it polished a skull
it had collected from one of the ill-fated

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:33.960
operatives.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:38.370
The Predator was a member of a species called
the Yautja, one of the few details about its

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:41.389
race that DiLiegro’s files hadn’t mentioned.

00:07:41.389 --> 00:07:45.889
Everything else was accurate though, it was
indeed a hunter, here to claim trophies as

00:07:45.889 --> 00:07:50.759
proof of its skill; these trophies happened
to be the skulls and spines of whatever it

00:07:50.759 --> 00:07:51.759
killed.

00:07:51.759 --> 00:07:55.620
Hearing the sound of an incoming vehicle,
the Predator instinctively reached for a control

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.520
on its left wrist gauntlet.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:01.870
Its cloaking device reactivated, bending the
light away from itself to render the alien

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.819
hunter nearly invisible.

00:08:03.819 --> 00:08:08.710
Through the lenses of its bio mask, the Predator
watched the craft pass overhead, and the shape

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:14.120
of a single, humanoid heat signature dropping
from it and landing in the rainforest.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:18.419
Trekking through the lush vegetation, Able
walked towards the location he had been given.

00:08:18.419 --> 00:08:22.360
It always irked the immortal barbarian when
the Foundation attempted to use him to perform

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.139
their menial dirty work.

00:08:24.139 --> 00:08:26.639
To Able, such tasks were beneath him.

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:31.039
But he had been promised a fight with a worthy
adversary, and that was the only reason he

00:08:31.039 --> 00:08:33.540
had agreed to undertake this mission.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:37.590
Looking around as he reached a clearing, there
was no sign of the MTF agents.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:41.669
Until, that is, Able craned his neck upwards
and found them.

00:08:41.669 --> 00:08:45.519
Something had meticulously gathered up the
bodies and hung them from the branches by

00:08:45.519 --> 00:08:46.649
their legs.

00:08:46.649 --> 00:08:51.790
It felt distinctly like a warning, as well
as a taunting gloat; every indicator pointed

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:56.050
to this being the action of a creature that
was marking its newfound territory.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:09:01.519
With a wave of his hand, Able pulled a black-edged
sword out of a pocket dimension holding his

00:09:01.519 --> 00:09:04.570
weapons, holding the blade at the ready.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:08.740
Looking down, he saw three points of red light
had appeared on his bare chest.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:13.230
Just as Able caught sight of the treetop where
the lasers were coming from, a bolt of high-energy

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:15.339
plasma was fired towards him.

00:09:15.339 --> 00:09:19.550
Within the same split second, he hurled his
sword in the direction of his invisible enemy.

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:23.360
The blast struck him and knocked him down,
searing his flesh – not that Able could

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:24.610
feel the pain.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:27.930
At the same time, his sword spun through the
air and cleaved through the branch where the

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:32.540
Predator had been perched, causing the creature
to drop to the jungle floor with a thud.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:37.820
As the Yautja stood up, it noticed its gauntlet
was sparking, having sustained damage in the

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:38.820
fall.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:40.910
Now, its cloaking device was flickering on
and off.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:45.060
The Predator knew it would need to repair
its equipment, but first and foremost needed

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.600
to collect a trophy from its latest kill.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.930
The creature strode towards where Able was
laying, a scorch mark left by the plasma caster

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.820
burned into his flesh.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:58.019
Its cloaking device still malfunctioning,
the hunter reached down to claim its prize…

00:09:58.019 --> 00:10:02.190
Able’s eyes suddenly snapped open and caught
the creature by surprise.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:06.600
Reeling his leg back, he delivered a sharp
kick that sent the Predator hurtling backward,

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:11.170
despite it being well over seven feet tall
and five-hundred-and-twenty pounds of armor

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.089
and alien muscle.

00:10:13.089 --> 00:10:17.660
Able hurriedly stood back up, facing off against
the alien warrior as it too drew itself to

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:18.769
full height.

00:10:18.769 --> 00:10:22.800
The gauntlet on its left wrist continued to
spit sparks, until the Predator reached a

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.510
clawed digit over and pressed a control.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:30.410
With an electronic bleep, the cloak deactivated
fully, and the hunter was revealed.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:34.260
It was tall, standing on two legs like a man.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:39.360
It seemed lithe and agile but clearly almost
as strong as Able himself, judging by how

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.100
muscular it was.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:46.140
Long appendages resembling locks of hair protruded
from its head, behind a metal faceplate, a

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:48.850
mask covering the true face of the creature
below.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:53.780
A clicking, chittering noise emanated from
beneath the Predator’s bio mask, as it reached

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:58.870
for a sash that went across its front, and
produced a pair of small metal circles.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:01.839
Able flexed his shoulders and ran at the creature.

00:11:01.839 --> 00:11:06.410
The Predator hurled both its disks at Able,
curved blades extending from both of them

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:08.230
as they spun through the air.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:12.670
Able ducked out of the path of one shuriken,
narrowly dodging the second as he charged

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.260
at the alien hunter.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:19.139
Reaching for its back, the Predator produced
the long, ornate handle of its combi stick.

00:11:19.139 --> 00:11:23.519
Both ends of the telescopic spear extended
and the hunter began racing forward to clash

00:11:23.519 --> 00:11:26.010
head-on with its newfound prey.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:29.779
It plunged the spear right through Able with
all of its strength, lifting the barbarian

00:11:29.779 --> 00:11:31.990
off his feet on the end of its weapon.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:37.600
Out of nowhere, SCP-076 produced another of
his swords, the Predator turning to look in

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:42.720
confusion at the weapon that had seemingly
just appeared in the hand of what it had taken

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.710
for an ordinary human.

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:49.510
Catching the off-world game hunter by surprise,
Able swept the sword through the air, cleaving

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:54.430
the creature’s spear in two, causing him
to drop back to the ground, landing on his

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:55.430
feet.

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:58.790
Following it with a second, swift swing of
his blade, Able brought the weapon down in

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:01.470
a slash that cut across the creature’s chest.

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:05.541
It sliced through the thick, reptilian hide
of the Predator, leaving a streak of oozing,

00:12:05.541 --> 00:12:08.570
florescent green blood oozing from its torso.

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:13.480
The creature roared in pain, a sound like
the call of a lion echoing through the trees.

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:18.560
In retaliation, the Predator extended a pair
of blades contained in its right gauntlet

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:20.320
and swiped them at Able.

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:24.620
The wrist blades narrowly missed his face
as he dodged in incoming attack, only to be

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.810
caught by the creature’s other hand.

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:31.310
It gripped his head and plunged downwards,
knocking Able over and sending him face-first

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.430
into the rainforest floor.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:37.269
Reaching for its cloaking device control,
the Predator disappeared, retreating into

00:12:37.269 --> 00:12:39.880
the jungle to tend to its heavily bleeding
wound.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:43.040
“What manner of devil is this creature,
Hall?”

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:47.080
Able yelled at the researcher over his earpiece,
hacking branches out of his path with his

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:50.870
sword as he followed the trail of luminous
green left by the wounded hunter.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.589
“It’s a warrior from another world,”
Hall replied.

00:12:53.589 --> 00:12:56.769
“A hunter that tracks its prey by their
body heat.

00:12:56.769 --> 00:13:01.079
Considers itself honorable, but often likes
to go after more dangerous targets to challenge

00:13:01.079 --> 00:13:02.079
itself.

00:13:02.079 --> 00:13:03.090
Not unlike you, Able.”

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:05.519
“I am nothing like this demon!”

00:13:05.519 --> 00:13:07.149
the barbarian shouted in fury.

00:13:07.149 --> 00:13:09.709
“This gutless monster has no honor.

00:13:09.709 --> 00:13:14.260
If it did, it would not give itself such an
unfair advantage, nor would it run away when

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:15.260
wounded.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:19.470
A true warrior would be happy to die a warrior’s
death in single combat, and wouldn’t rely

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:21.490
on all its fancy weaponry.”

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:25.310
“Well, from what we can tell, these things
have their own code of sorts,” DiLiegro’s

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:27.029
voice said over the comms.

00:13:27.029 --> 00:13:31.959
“You might not think of this hunter as honorable,
but it definitely thinks of itself that way.

00:13:31.959 --> 00:13:33.270
Maybe use that to your advantage?”

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:36.850
“I do not need to be lectured by the likes
of you!”

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:37.850
Able interrupted.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:41.699
“You have not known the heat of battle,
none of you at the Foundation have.

00:13:41.699 --> 00:13:47.180
I will follow the trail of this cowardly beast’s
blood, and cleave its foul head from its shoulders!”

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:51.130
Unbeknownst to Able, high above on a branch,
the Predator was watching him.

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:56.290
Its bio mask had been zoomed in on him, the
hunter listening in to the barbarian’s outrage.

00:13:56.290 --> 00:14:00.899
It turned to the task at hand, opening up
its MediKit and producing the surgical tools

00:14:00.899 --> 00:14:04.630
within as it tended to the deep green cut
across its chest.

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:09.589
Stifling roars of pain beneath its mask, the
Predator stapled the injury closed and applied

00:14:09.589 --> 00:14:11.560
a solvent to cauterize it.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:16.350
Night was beginning to fall, and Able had
long since lost the trail of green blood.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:20.820
Frustrated, he thought back to what the puny
researchers at the Foundation had told him

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:22.750
of his alien adversary.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:27.220
If it believed itself to be honorable, to
have a code, then perhaps using that to lure

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:29.970
it out to face him might work.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:34.720
With the sun rapidly disappearing beyond the
treeline, Able gathered a number of branches,

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:39.340
hacking them off trees with his sword and
fashioning them into burning torches.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:44.769
He placed them in a circle around the circumference
of a clearing, creating a makeshift gladiatorial

00:14:44.769 --> 00:14:45.769
arena.

00:14:45.769 --> 00:14:51.029
He could feel his blood boiling, the urge
to defeat this monster making him seethe.

00:14:51.029 --> 00:14:55.550
Throwing his head back and beating a fist
against his chest, Able roared up at the dark

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:56.550
sky.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:58.529
“Come out, hunter!” he howled.

00:14:58.529 --> 00:14:59.529
“Show yourself!

00:14:59.529 --> 00:15:01.519
Come on, do it.

00:15:01.519 --> 00:15:03.570
I’m right here!”

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:08.180
Watching him from afar, hidden by its cloak,
the Predator recognized what was happening.

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:12.320
This was a challenge, a direct call to engage
in single combat.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:16.589
Refusing this challenge and shooting its prey
dead would be quicker, easier, but the hunter

00:15:16.589 --> 00:15:19.610
knew it was being watched, and therefore judged.

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:23.400
With a growl, it dropped to the ground and
paced towards the circle.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:27.740
Able turned as the Predator revealed itself,
appearing almost from thin air.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:31.449
As it did, he drew one of his weapons and
stood ready to fight.

00:15:31.449 --> 00:15:35.620
The hunter shrugged off the technology it
carried on its back, dropping the plasma caster

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:39.529
and the MediKit, before reaching up and pulling
off its mask.

00:15:39.529 --> 00:15:44.880
Its face was grotesque, four hooked mandibles
surrounding its mouth, flared in anger.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:49.889
“You are one ugly-” Able said, only to
be interrupted by the Predator extending the

00:15:49.889 --> 00:15:53.670
blades from its gauntlet and letting out another
bestial roar.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:57.730
Holding his sword aloft, Able gave a goading
beckon to his opponent as the pair of them

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.130
circled one another.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:03.680
Finally, the creature gave in and lunged at
him, swiping its pair of razor-sharp serrated

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:04.940
blades at Able.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:09.860
He swung his sword in at the last second,
deflecting the oncoming blow with a clang

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:10.880
of metal.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:15.329
Reaching into his pocket dimension, Able pulled
a second weapon out in his other hand, and

00:16:15.329 --> 00:16:18.880
swiped it at the Predator, slicing through
the creature’s hide and leaving another

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:21.200
gaping wound at its thigh.

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:24.050
Roaring in fury, the Predator launched another
strike.

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:28.600
Able blocked the attack yet again, this time
by crossing his swords, but the Predator barged

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:33.670
forward, driving its blades into its prey’s
chest and pinning his two weapons against

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:34.670
him.

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:38.480
The monstrous alien viciously head-butted
Able, the hooks of its mandibles scratching

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:43.130
his face as it did, before reaching up to
the back of his neck with its free hand.

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:46.970
Able could feel the sheer strength of the
hunter lifting him off his feet, ready to

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:50.800
twist his neck and pull his head off to claim
it as a trophy.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:54.829
Kicking the Predator in the chest, Able used
the force of the impact to push himself free

00:16:54.829 --> 00:16:59.290
from the creature’s grip, backflipping through
the air and landing a few feet away.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:03.400
His swords clattered together as they dropped
to the ground, the immortal barbarian summoning

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:06.169
another and immediately charging at the Predator.

00:17:06.169 --> 00:17:10.480
It had been winded by the kick, and barely
recovered in time to defend itself as the

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.319
blade swung for its neck.

00:17:12.319 --> 00:17:17.029
The Predator staggered back, green blood oozing
from its hide and pouring from its mouth.

00:17:17.029 --> 00:17:19.000
That blow had mortally wounded it.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.610
It was bleeding heavily, and knew it might
not survive this hunt.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:27.819
But it refused to be bested by a human, even
one as seemingly invulnerable as Able.

00:17:27.819 --> 00:17:32.510
Hunching over, listening to him slowly approaching
to deliver the killing blow, the Predator

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:37.350
tapped a series of controls on its gauntlet;
a gradually-accelerating beeping began emanating

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:38.820
from the device.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:43.419
Turning around at the last second, the alien
hunter impaled Able before he was upon it,

00:17:43.419 --> 00:17:47.240
skewering SCP-076-2 on its wrist blades.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:51.470
His sword had been raised above his head to
plunge through the creature, and even while

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:55.120
impaled, Able was able to deliver the final
blow.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:59.830
Stabbing the Predator while it too had stabbed
him, the pair were locked in a stalemate,

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:04.820
angrily roaring at each other until an explosion
of energy burst from the hunter’s gauntlets,

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:08.590
reducing both Able and the Predator to atoms.

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:11.330
Watching from their satellite feed, Hall and
DiLiegro sighed.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:15.760
They wouldn’t have their specimen for testing,
but at least they knew that Able would eventually

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:20.100
resurrect within the stone cube, SCP-076-1.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:23.679
But even higher up than their satellite, someone
else was watching.

00:18:23.679 --> 00:18:28.110
A group of Predators growled and chittered
amongst themselves, having witnessed from

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:31.720
their ship as one of their own had died in
battle with Able.

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:35.500
Although there was no way of knowing, the
noises the hunting party were making could

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:39.150
have been expressions of disappointment at
their fallen brother…

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:44.390
or a declaration of war.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:52.200
Now go and check out “BOBA FETT VS SCP-610
THE FLESH THAT HATES”.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:59.390
And afterwards, witness a battle between two
brothers in “SCP-073 &amp; 076 CAIN VS ABLE”!

